# =============================================================================
# ServeOS Caddy layout (serveos-production-proxy)
#
#   /etc/caddy/Caddyfile          # central config — import sites only
#   /etc/caddy/sites/serveos.caddy
#   /etc/caddy/sites/whats-auto.caddy
#   /etc/caddy/sites/app3.caddy
#   /etc/caddy/sites/app4.caddy
#
# Do NOT put Whats Auto routes in the main Caddyfile.
# Do NOT replace serveos.caddy or other site files.
# Do NOT add a second Caddy container or bind 80/443 from Whats Auto.
# =============================================================================
#
# 1) Central Caddyfile (/etc/caddy/Caddyfile) should contain:
#
#    import /etc/caddy/sites/*.caddy
#
#    Keep any existing global options (email, log, etc.) above that line.
#
# 2) Make this repo file visible inside the Caddy container as
#    /etc/caddy/sites/whats-auto.caddy
#
#    Option A — bind-mount this file (add to serveos-production-proxy, then recreate):
#
#      /var/www/whats-auto/deploy/contabo/whats-auto.caddy:/etc/caddy/sites/whats-auto.caddy:ro
#      /var/www/whats-auto/apps/backend/media:/var/www/whats-auto/apps/backend/media:ro
#
#    Option B — if ServeOS already mounts a host `sites/` dir to /etc/caddy/sites,
#    copy or symlink into that directory:
#
#      cp /var/www/whats-auto/deploy/contabo/whats-auto.caddy /path/to/serveos/sites/whats-auto.caddy
#
#    New volumes need a proxy recreate once. Reload is enough after file edits.
#
# 3) Reload (does not restart the VPS):
#
#    docker exec serveos-production-proxy caddy reload \
#      --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile --adapter caddyfile
